      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ZAYYANO (8) has attracted solid market support at his recent starts without breaking through, but his latest fourth at Grafton suggested a win isn't far away. Dropping back in trip could be the key, and in a race of this nature he looks well placed to finally open his account. SIR DON (6) produced an honest effort when finishing fourth over 1125m at Grafton last start and should strip fitter for this assignment. With even luck, he shapes as one of the main each-way dangers. MILDURA LAD (5) was not far away in the run at this track last time out, and he looks suited by the rise in distance. He has a genuine each-way chance with further improvement expected. YONAKA (7) has been well supported at his past couple of outings without delivering, but he has gone close to winning a race in the past. He is worth including in all combos, especially starting from the pole position. DIVINE MANDATE (3) makes his debut from the Paul Shailer stable with the blinkers on for the first time. Each way.",
